WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.219
First gentleman: I say! This Old Interest 'victory' parade is

cue-2
00:00:04.219 --> 00:00:09.420
the best show I've been to in quite some
time! Ha! That's what I call 'An Election

cue-3
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:13.940
Entertainment'!
Second gentleman: Absolutely! And when our side

cue-4
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.599
challenges the result in parliament, it
can only end one way. Parliament is full

cue-5
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.600
of New Interest supporters – we've got the
majority there! When there's

cue-6
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.679
disagreement over the result of an
election, it's parliament that has the

cue-7
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.739
final say!
First gentleman: Yes, quite! And then this 'True Blue

cue-8
00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:35.940
Triumph' will vanish into thin air as if it
never was! Let's enjoy the spectacle

cue-9
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.619
while we can!

cue-10
00:00:39.319 --> 00:00:40.540
The Duke: Indeed!

cue-11
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:47.799
It's just as you say. Friends in high
places, just like me, the Duke of

cue-12
00:00:47.799 --> 00:00:54.339
Newcastle – that's what counts. How does
the saying go? 'The

cue-13
00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:59.880
ambitious Peer, the Knight, the 'Squire, can
buy the election they

cue-14
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:06.739
desire'. So reflect, my friends, and judge
from thence, How

cue-15
00:01:06.739 --> 00:01:13.500
idle this extreme expense; What mighty
sums are thrown away,

cue-16
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.879
To be the pageant of the day!
